Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:10:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] cross-stream: TALK: the S3 output lint skips register
 words whose first character pair is not in the line (same verdicts, tested
 against the original scan); S3-TALK speed

talk_safe.c is the TALK stream's: the lint read and scanned every register word for every
generated line, 80% of the 100 to 400 ms a line cost on the GBA. A 1,024-bit pair table,
the records read eight at a time, wordc inline. test_talk_lint_speed.c compares the verdict
with a copy of the old scan on every register word in ten templates.

